WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.890
Welcome to "Ear Biscuits,"

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.980
the podcast where two lifelong
friends talk about life

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.630
for a long time.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:10.463
I'm Link.

00:00:10.463 --> 00:00:11.296
And I'm Rhett.

00:00:11.296 --> 00:00:12.859
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:12.859 --> 00:00:17.859
we are catching up about our
little Thanksgiving times,

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.460
which ended up being unexpected.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.600
Catastrophic.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.040
In many different ways.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:23.873
For my body.

00:00:23.873 --> 00:00:26.403
But let's start with the
elephant in the room,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.980
which is your sling.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.540
You talking about Ned from Try Guys?

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.373
Oh.

00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:32.670
Well, I know what you're doing.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.980
You're saying the Try Guys made a video

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:36.540
where they literally had
an elephant in the room

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.970
to address the Ned situation, which was-

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.020
To literally cover him up.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.073
Which was clever.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.133
No.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:45.450
Link has a sling on for
those of you listening.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.860
A Link sling.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.480
His arm is in a sling.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.563
It's my right arm.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.140
Oh me.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.110
So, this was two days ago.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.430
You know, this is a Tuesday.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:57.360
Fresh, fresh.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.790
That was a Sunday morning.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:00.960
And man, it had been a while

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.700
since I've been on my mountain bike, dude.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.021
I mean, like before Thanksgiving,

00:01:05.021 --> 00:01:06.854
I just hadn't been out there.

00:01:06.854 --> 00:01:11.854
I hadn't been hitting the
pedals, you know, as they say.

00:01:12.062 --> 00:01:14.940
Hitting the slopes of the...

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.830
That's not the right sport.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:17.663
Anyway-

00:01:17.663 --> 00:01:18.930
You were doing an awesome trick.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.763
Big jump.

00:01:19.763 --> 00:01:20.700
No.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.570
I-

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:22.470
Were you by yourself?

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.700
I was by myself.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.990
I was doing my big run that I like to do.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.370
It's like a two hour run,

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.787
and I was like, "It's been a while.

00:01:30.787 --> 00:01:32.160
"I don't know if I can do this."

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.177
And then, but I was like, you know,

00:01:33.177 --> 00:01:36.720
you can turn around at any point
'cause it's an up and back.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.274
Right.

00:01:38.274 --> 00:01:42.060
And I'm going up, I get
to the first saddle,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.470
I'm feeling good.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.630
So, I'm like, I'm starting to feel myself.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:48.780
And so, I'm going up to the next saddle,

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.814
which is, you know, the
main turnaround point

00:01:51.814 --> 00:01:55.147
that then you have this
long ride all the way down,

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.670
which is super nice.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:01.670
And, you know, I'm listening to my music.

00:02:02.248 --> 00:02:05.010
And I'm, I get to this one point-

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.210
Is that advised?

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.043
Yeah.

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:08.297
I mean, I usually listen
to a podcast going up

00:02:08.297 --> 00:02:11.130
'cause it's so slow going up.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.570
And then I listen to music going down.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.790
AirPod Pros?

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:15.690
Yeah, why?

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.332
Well, so you do the thing

00:02:17.332 --> 00:02:19.500
where you can hear the
environment as well?

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.490
You don't put on noise
canceling when you ride?

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.323
I do, yeah.

00:02:22.323 --> 00:02:23.400
You put on noise canceling?

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.900
Yeah.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.580
Just so, I mean, if something,

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:31.580
if something pops out that's
not like a consistent tone,

00:02:31.788 --> 00:02:32.871
you'll still hear it.

00:02:32.871 --> 00:02:35.329
That's how noise canceling works.

00:02:35.329 --> 00:02:36.162
Okay.

00:02:36.162 --> 00:02:37.030
For the most part.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:38.940
That's why you can,

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.400
well, that didn't have a factor here

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:44.220
if you're trying to like get ahead of me.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.150
But I'm going uphill.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.110
I mean, like, the dangerous
part is coming downhill.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.360
And, you know, the irony
of this is kind of crazy.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.550
Like, right before Thanksgiving break,

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.470
we recorded a "Car Biscuit."

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.700
If you don't know,

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.820
that's when we basically do a version

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.560
of "Ear Biscuits" from-

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.393
A car.

00:03:02.393 --> 00:03:04.710
Either my car or Rhett's car.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.450
Exclusive to the Mythical Society.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.450
Yeah, so every month?

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.770
Every month we do one of those.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:11.603
We do.

00:03:11.603 --> 00:03:13.290
And I always have fun doing those.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.300
We never know what we're gonna talk about.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.585
It's like "Ear Biscuits"
but even less curated.

00:03:19.585 --> 00:03:21.300
So, you might be into that.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.133
Right.

00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:23.780
The last, the one that's like...

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.740
It's either about to come
out or it just came out.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.090
We recorded right before Thanksgiving,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.490
and we ended up talking about like,

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.460
what are the things that we do

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.950
that are most likely to injure us.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.200
And I was like, it has to
be mountain biking for me.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.294
Yeah, that's what started it.

00:03:41.294 --> 00:03:44.520
What's most likely to kill
you or what's most dangerous.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.585
But yeah, we concluded
that between the two of us,

00:03:47.585 --> 00:03:50.640
you were more regularly doing
the more dangerous thing,

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.770
which was mountain biking,
the most dangerous thing.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.490
And I, so, I mean, is
that like manifesting it?

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:00.330
I don't, I think I
believe in manifestation.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.830
Okay, well, did you...

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.240
Did it, okay.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.630
Did it cross your mind at
any point before the injury

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.800
that we had had that conversation?

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.660
No, and I think that's the problem.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.860
I don't think it had any impact then.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.630
Coming down the hill is the part

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:16.711
where it's like you gotta be on your toes.

00:04:16.711 --> 00:04:21.711
You gotta be, you gotta
really be on guard.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:24.053
But going up, it's like,
you can kind of zone out.

00:04:24.053 --> 00:04:26.520
You can kind of, you
know, listen to a podcast.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:30.450
You're just cranking away,
going in like this granny gear.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.302
But then there's this one
place where it does dip down,

00:04:33.302 --> 00:04:35.280
and you get a little rest,

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.218
and like so it's a slight decline.

00:04:38.218 --> 00:04:40.180
And instead of listening
to a podcast this time,

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:42.780
I was listening to music on the way up.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.320
And I was really happy
that I was doing so well.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.610
Okay.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.779
So, I just, I really cranked it.

00:04:49.779 --> 00:04:51.329
Do you know what song it was?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.790
It was a, it was Freddie Gibbs.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.690
I don't know which song.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.400
What was the BPM do you believe?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.613
It was probably 98.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.283
That's kind of slow.

00:05:04.283 --> 00:05:06.485
It's not too fast, but I'm cranking it.

00:05:06.485 --> 00:05:07.568
Okay.

00:05:07.568 --> 00:05:08.401
And...

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.359
I just, I guess I just
hit this little divot.

00:05:15.359 --> 00:05:17.817
And I wasn't present.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:20.223
I just wasn't totally present.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.053
And typically when you fall,

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:30.423
you can kind of catch yourself.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.270
A lot of times I kind of know it's coming.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:34.440
Like, I mean, once-

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.240
You mean without fully falling?

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.336
No, falling but like
getting your hands out

00:05:39.336 --> 00:05:40.680
and like catching yourself.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.080
And like I'm wearing gloves,
I'm wearing elbow pads,

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:45.210
I'm wearing knee pads,
I'm wearing a helmet.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:47.913
I'm wearing all these
things because I do fall.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.990
But this was really unusual.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:55.440
I mean, my front tire,

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:59.370
I think it just took a
really hard, boom, right turn

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.310
right when it hit this divot.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.480
Wham!

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:06.266
And then it just tossed me.

00:06:06.266 --> 00:06:09.180
I would say it slammed
me more than tossed me

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.210
over the right side of the bike.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.070
My forward momentum took me over,

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:18.390
and it happened so fast
that I did not have time

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:22.600
to get my hand, my right
hand off the handlebar

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.630
to put my hand in front
of me, and kind of,

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.070
so that my hand would be the first thing

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.540
that hit the ground.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:32.910
So, I was diving,

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:36.420
and my right shoulder was-

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:37.410
The first thing that hit?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.666
I dropped it.

00:06:38.666 --> 00:06:42.374
And so, the first thing
that hit was the top

00:06:42.374 --> 00:06:44.332
of my right shoulder.

00:06:44.332 --> 00:06:45.810
Bam!

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:46.890
Into the ground.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.290
And then it was like the
side of my face I think.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.414
Like, or the side of
my helmet or something.

00:06:51.414 --> 00:06:53.703
But I really did, I didn't hit my head.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:55.763
I didn't.

00:06:55.763 --> 00:06:56.596
I'm...

00:06:56.596 --> 00:06:57.429
I didn't.

00:06:57.429 --> 00:06:58.920
Do I sound convincing?
You sound

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.140
like you might not
remember, so maybe you did.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:02.580
I mean, 'cause that's a big concern.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.413
But...

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:08.250
So, it was like a mouse trap, dude.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.140
It was just like wham!

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:10.973
You know?

00:07:10.973 --> 00:07:11.806
And...

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:16.230
So, I'm on my right side.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:17.880
What's the first thought?

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.773
First thought is,

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.610
have I dislocated my shoulder?

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.260
So, I'm like

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:29.130
And I like get off the
ground a little bit,

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.870
and I raised my right arm.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:34.500
And so, there was a little bit
of mental relief that like,

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.120
okay, I can raise my right arm.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.206
I went like this, just raised it.

00:07:38.206 --> 00:07:40.500
And I was like, okay, my
arm is still in the socket

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:41.610
because the way that it hit,

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.380
I just felt like it could have

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.410
just taken it all the way out.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:49.770
And my shoulders, you know,
I have some shoulder issues,

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:51.104
so it's kind of,

00:07:51.104 --> 00:07:54.062
it's been historically a little weak

00:07:54.062 --> 00:07:56.130
in keeping it in socket,

00:07:56.130 --> 00:08:00.510
so I just didn't want to have
to do the lethal weapon thing

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:02.760
where like you hit your
shoulder against the ground

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.950
or like your bike or something
to put it back in socket.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:05.790
That was my first thought.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:08.167
How far into the process did you think,

00:08:08.167 --> 00:08:10.320
"I'm gonna talk about
this on the podcast?"

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:14.491
My second thought was I
have to get off this trail

00:08:14.491 --> 00:08:17.310
'cause I know that there's
some mountain bikers

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.050
that have passed me

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.760
and some that are
probably just coming down,

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.920
and they can come down pretty fast.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.810
They have to turn around usually.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:25.650
You don't wanna pile up?

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.270
I don't want to get hit

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.714
or I don't wanna send
somebody off the mountain.

00:08:29.714 --> 00:08:33.480
So like, then I'm like scooting
to the side of the trail.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:37.680
And so, on my left side,
I'm going up the mountain,

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.220
on my left side it's
like a decent drop off.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.093
One that if I sent somebody
careening off of it-

00:08:43.093 --> 00:08:45.930
They would do more than
dislocate their shoulder?

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:46.800
Yeah.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:50.820
And on the right it's just
a slope and some thickets.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.630
So, I just like, I'm like
trying to sit in the thicket

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.570
and not panic, and this is
all happening pretty quickly.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.040
So, that was my second thought.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.993
And then my third thought was,

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.650
I'm not, like,

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.990
I've been thinking about
going back to the gym

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.960
and now I'm gonna have
to shoot the show, GMM,

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.020
with like a sling and like...

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:13.853
Yeah.

00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:16.080
And 'cause I think I had assumed

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.593
that nothing was dislocated
so I'd broken something.

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:22.740
I think I pretty much knew at that point.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.500
Like, it was hurting.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:27.633
And, you know, that thing where like,

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:29.910
like I could move my
fingers, I raised my arm,

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:34.080
but then like as like in minute
two, it was like I really,

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:36.840
my body wouldn't let
me move my arm at all.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.673
You know?

00:09:37.673 --> 00:09:40.473
So, it just kind of like, it
knows something that I don't.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:47.370
and then I'm like, "Oh gosh."

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:50.970
And, you know, I didn't think
about telling the story yet.

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:53.617
I was just, 'cause then I kind
of went in an almost like,

00:09:53.617 --> 00:09:55.020
"Don't freak out, don't freak out."

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.437
Like, I started like taking some-

00:09:56.437 --> 00:09:58.650
"Don't freak out," as
in, what do you mean?

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:02.040
Like, I was afraid to look at my shoulder.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.840
I was afraid I was gonna faint.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.490
You're afraid you're gonna
have a panic attack up there?

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:06.570
Yeah, yeah.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:07.620
Or just, yeah.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.482
So, like I felt a little faint.

00:10:09.482 --> 00:10:13.590
I was like, just like pouring sweat.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:17.227
I was already pouring sweat,
but like, it was that like,

00:10:17.227 --> 00:10:19.197
"Don't pass out."

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.820
And then one runner comes down.

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.293
Or maybe it was a cyclist.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:27.680
Was like, "Dude, are you okay?"

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.723
And I was like, "Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:30.723 --> 00:10:31.717
"I'll be fine.

00:10:31.717 --> 00:10:32.550
"I just took a fall.

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:33.383
"I'm gonna have to recover."

00:10:33.383 --> 00:10:34.717
So, it was just like, my
instinct was just like,

00:10:34.717 --> 00:10:35.784
"Yeah, I'm okay.

00:10:35.784 --> 00:10:36.617
"Just keep going."

00:10:36.617 --> 00:10:37.950
"I'll be fine."

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:42.158
And then it was like
another couple of minutes,

00:10:42.158 --> 00:10:47.158
and there was another runner that came by,

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.490
and she was like, "Are you okay?"

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:53.630
And I'm like, "I took...

00:10:54.727 --> 00:10:55.567
"Yeah.

00:10:55.567 --> 00:10:58.830
"I just need to gather myself."

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:01.260
So, what is your definition of okay?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.147
And then she-

00:11:02.147 --> 00:11:03.520
'Cause I'm questioning that at this point.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.100
Yeah, I looked up at her-

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.270
Like, what did you mean by that?

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:07.103
And I was like-

00:11:07.103 --> 00:11:08.670
Yeah, like, "I'm not dying."

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:13.050
I didn't want to inconvenience anybody.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:15.990
You didn't want this woman to
have to put you on her back?

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.100
Right.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.663
Sherpa me down the mountain.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:23.820
But then I looked up at
her, and she wasn't leaving.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:24.653
She knew.

00:11:24.653 --> 00:11:26.190
And I was like-

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:27.023
He is not okay.

00:11:27.023 --> 00:11:27.903
"I'm not okay.

00:11:28.867 --> 00:11:32.103
"I think I've broken my collarbone.

00:11:33.607 --> 00:11:38.220
"I need just to sit
here for a little bit."

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:39.690
Oh man, I wish I could talk to this woman.

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.527
And she was like, "You know,
I can just take you down.

00:11:41.527 --> 00:11:42.787
"I can take you down to the saddle.

00:11:42.787 --> 00:11:43.987
"There's more mountain bikers.

00:11:43.987 --> 00:11:45.789
"Like, we can, you know,

00:11:45.789 --> 00:11:48.030
"you can get some help or whatever."

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.980
I was like, "Okay, yeah."

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.663
And then so I sat there, and
then she like stood beside me.

00:11:52.663 --> 00:11:57.663
And I was doing some deep breathing.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:02.060
And then occasionally she
would ask me questions like...

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.880
I can't remember, but she
started talking to me.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.480
Do you think she was an angel?

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.570
I think she was an angel, yes.

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:11.490
I think she was my guardian angel.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.050
Did you get her number?

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:14.520
I mean, not like, did
you get her number, like-

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.450
I mean, I'm not-
Are you gonna stay

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.500
in touch with this woman?

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.593
I mean, do you have to be Christian

00:12:17.593 --> 00:12:18.676
to have a guardian angel?

00:12:18.676 --> 00:12:21.134
Can you be a Buddhist and
have a guardian angel?

00:12:21.134 --> 00:12:22.270
Can you be anybody?

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:25.175
I know you can be a member
of the band Alabama,

00:12:25.175 --> 00:12:27.275
but I think that they're pretty Christian.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.180
But you're not gonna stay
in touch with this woman

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.830
who saved you?

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.510
There's more to this story, my friend.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:34.343
Okay, all right.

00:12:34.343 --> 00:12:35.176
Okay, all right.

00:12:35.176 --> 00:12:36.009
I'm just...

00:12:36.009 --> 00:12:36.870
So-

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:37.703
'Cause a lot of times
you can't get in touch

00:12:37.703 --> 00:12:38.760
with an angel.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:39.869
Right, they don't have phones.

00:12:39.869 --> 00:12:41.820
You call the number and it
just is like not in service.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.785
They give you a number, but it's a-

00:12:43.785 --> 00:12:44.868
Every time that's happened to me-

00:12:44.868 --> 00:12:45.701
It's bullshit.

00:12:45.701 --> 00:12:46.534
That's what's happened.

00:12:46.534 --> 00:12:47.367
It's that angel fake.

00:12:47.367 --> 00:12:48.840
Yeah.

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:51.908
It took me 15 minutes
to be able to get up.

00:12:51.908 --> 00:12:53.190
Like, to be able to stand up.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.023
Right, yeah.

00:12:54.023 --> 00:12:56.250
I was not doing good.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.780
And she was like, "Do you
have something to eat?"

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:01.080
And I had like one of
these kids bars that like,

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.300
it has more sugar than
a normal protein bar,

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.739
which was nice 'cause I needed that.

00:13:04.739 --> 00:13:06.427
So, I took a bite and then I was like,

00:13:06.427 --> 00:13:08.790
"Oh god, I'm gonna vomit."

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:11.037
But then I did eat like a third of it,

00:13:11.037 --> 00:13:13.917
and I'm like drinking my electrolyte water

00:13:13.917 --> 00:13:15.904
and like trying to just
gather myself, you know?

00:13:15.904 --> 00:13:17.362
You had a lot of things.

00:13:17.362 --> 00:13:18.195
Yeah.

00:13:18.195 --> 00:13:19.560
You were prepared.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:20.760
You know I have some stuff.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:21.870
I would've been over there with nothing.

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:23.043
Yeah yeah.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:27.485
And my bike was okay,

00:13:27.485 --> 00:13:30.480
but like the freaking bell on my bike,

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.880
like there's a bell on the
left side of the handlebar,

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.410
that thing was obliterated

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.192
and just in the middle of the trail.

00:13:37.192 --> 00:13:38.523
Like, my bike took a hard licking too.

00:13:38.523 --> 00:13:40.500
You lost your bell?

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.720
Well, I was like, "Can you get my bell?"

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:45.600
And then I put it in my pocket.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.232
And...

00:13:47.232 --> 00:13:48.990
Must be a nice bell.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:51.148
I've learned to not leave
the scene of an accident

00:13:51.148 --> 00:13:56.148
without looking around
because in falls before,

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:59.820
if I'm okay, like I'll just
get on my bike and start riding

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.800
and realize there's something
that's fallen off my bike

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.350
and I gotta go back and get it.

00:14:04.746 --> 00:14:06.329
So, I finally got up, and I was like,

00:14:06.329 --> 00:14:10.987
"I can't get my bike down this mountain.

00:14:10.987 --> 00:14:11.910
"I can't."

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:12.743
You know, she's like,

00:14:12.743 --> 00:14:14.107
"I can push your bike down the mountain.

00:14:14.107 --> 00:14:14.940
"That's not a problem.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:15.870
"We'll just walk down."

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.770
I was like, "Thank you
so much for doing this."

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.230
I was just really appreciative.

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.826
And then like well, we
started walking down,

00:14:21.826 --> 00:14:25.284
and, you know, it dawned on me.

00:14:25.284 --> 00:14:27.117
It was like, if she didn't stop,

00:14:27.117 --> 00:14:29.850
only one other runner went by,

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:31.470
and it was a guy who was running

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:33.660
with such intensity going up the mountain

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:36.570
that he passed me running
going up the mountain

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:37.860
and I'm on a bike.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:38.760
Oh.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:40.200
So, like this guy ran back down.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.031
He was the only other guy that came by.

00:14:42.031 --> 00:14:44.910
And I just wouldn't have had
the nerve to ask him to help.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.020
That's what I told her.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.947
I was like, "I don't know
how I would've gotten down

00:14:47.947 --> 00:14:49.535
"'cause you're my only hope.

00:14:49.535 --> 00:14:51.177
"You're my guardian angel."

00:14:52.368 --> 00:14:55.451
And when I said that, she,
poof, she disappeared.

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:03.200
So, Katie and I just started talking

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:06.450
because it took-

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:07.283
Yeah, wow.

00:15:07.283 --> 00:15:10.870
An hour to walk down the mountain

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:16.440
with her behind me and me
just like holding my arm

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:19.050
in the sling that we made from,

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.870
she had on two shirts, so
she took off her over shirt.

00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:22.703
She was prepared.

00:15:22.703 --> 00:15:24.916
She was like, I want to...

00:15:24.916 --> 00:15:28.083
You know, back before I
stood up, she was like,

00:15:29.167 --> 00:15:31.140
"We can make my shirt into a sling."

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.190
She was an angel.

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:33.630
Angels always have an extra shirt.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:34.727
The first thing I thought was,

00:15:34.727 --> 00:15:37.620
"You gonna go down this
mountain without a shirt?"

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.203
So, I like looked up at
her, she had two shirts.

00:15:39.203 --> 00:15:40.530
Listen, it was magic.

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:42.570
And what I'm telling you is that what,

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.580
she's gonna go running in two shirts?

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:45.413
No.

00:15:45.413 --> 00:15:46.246
An angel takes off one shirt,

00:15:46.246 --> 00:15:47.670
and there's another shirt under there

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.560
because they're operating
in a magical way.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.048
The layers conceal the wings.

00:15:51.048 --> 00:15:51.881
Yeah, it's like,

00:15:51.881 --> 00:15:54.810
"Okay, I'm gonna have to do
the shirt trick with this one."

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.922
Yeah, and then she turned
her shirt into a sling,

00:15:56.922 --> 00:15:58.590
which only an angel could do.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.630
So far the evidence is strong for angel.

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:02.130
Oh gosh, yes.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:03.485
Well, every time a bell rings,

00:16:03.485 --> 00:16:04.740
an angel gets its wings.

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:06.026
Dang it, that's right!
Oh!

00:16:06.026 --> 00:16:08.484
So, you're saying when I took the crash-

00:16:08.484 --> 00:16:09.317
That bell rang.

00:16:09.317 --> 00:16:10.650
It created the angel

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.450
that then saved me.
"It's a Wonderful Life."

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.816
Yes, you manifested an angel
with your freaking bell.

00:16:14.816 --> 00:16:15.692
I'm glad you kept it.

00:16:15.692 --> 00:16:17.163
It's a lucky bell.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.163
I kept it.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:22.440
So yeah, I mean, we're like best friends.

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.990
When I finally got home and
told Christy, I was like,

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:26.850
I told her about Katie,

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:29.400
and then later on I was like,
"Yeah, my best friend Julie."

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.227
And she was like, "I thought
you said her name was Katie?"

00:16:31.227 --> 00:16:33.714
You already forgot your
angel's first name.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:36.453
My best friend Julie.

00:16:37.643 --> 00:16:40.463
I mean, I told her when
we got back to the bottom

00:16:40.463 --> 00:16:44.970
after the hour, it just,
there's many places you can park

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:46.350
and the place that I park

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:49.878
to start my ride is not the
main place or the second place.

00:16:49.878 --> 00:16:54.330
It's the third place that
requires a final climb

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:56.374
right before you get back to your car.

00:16:56.374 --> 00:16:59.520
And it's just on the street
so people don't like to do it.

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:01.880
But she also parked up there.

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.780
Oh yeah, so yeah, she moved her car

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:06.023
while you were all walking
down with her mind.

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.700
Just other proof that she was an angel.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:09.533
Yeah, that's what I'm saying.

00:17:09.533 --> 00:17:10.786
It's clear.

00:17:10.786 --> 00:17:11.910
I mean, I don't think
even think she had a car

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:13.613
because once she put my bike on my,

00:17:13.613 --> 00:17:14.970
I mean, I couldn't do anything.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:15.803
Yeah, it was a fake car.

00:17:15.803 --> 00:17:17.997
She put my bike on the rack,
and then I get in the car,

00:17:17.997 --> 00:17:19.297
and she was like, "Can you drive?

00:17:19.297 --> 00:17:20.190
"Are you okay?"

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.540
Yeah, I'm driving.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.190
And then I drive past her,

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:25.620
and she's just walking down
the street like Bill Bixby

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.324
at the end of "The Hulk."

00:17:27.324 --> 00:17:28.907
And then I bet when I turned the corner,

00:17:28.907 --> 00:17:31.290
the wings popped out and she flew away.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:33.450
Getting into her "car."

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:34.781
Yeah, right.

00:17:34.781 --> 00:17:38.103
I did take a picture with
her because I was like,

00:17:39.067 --> 00:17:41.670
"Katie, I've gotta, I
gotta take a picture."

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:45.030
And I know I look happy,
but I am not happy.

00:17:45.030 --> 00:17:47.340
Like, that was my best fake smile.

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:50.420
And you're zooming in on
her to see if she's...

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.260
She's so angelic.

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:53.100
They do a good job

00:17:53.100 --> 00:17:54.960
of just making themselves
look like normal people.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.070
I mean, that's part of their deal.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:56.903
Right.

00:17:56.903 --> 00:17:59.697
I got to know everything
about her husband Ron.

00:17:59.697 --> 00:18:02.523
He's a bedroom DJ just like me.

00:18:02.523 --> 00:18:04.500
He's more into house music.

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:05.333
Really?

00:18:05.333 --> 00:18:06.166
Yeah.

00:18:06.166 --> 00:18:07.680
Works for Snapchat.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.980
We negotiated a new deal for Mythical.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.030
Oh, that's great.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:12.900
With Snapchat.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.010
She definitely looks like somebody

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.380
who could run up a mountain.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.700
She ran up the freaking mountain,

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.130
and then she walked my
bike down it for an hour.

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.590
And she's not sweaty at all.

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:23.494
And she was so gracious.

00:18:23.494 --> 00:18:28.494
I mean, it literally added
basically an hour to her day.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:30.660
So, I got her number.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.130
Yeah, but she's just doing her job.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.451
And I'm getting her mailing address,

00:18:34.451 --> 00:18:37.470
so I can send her some sort
of gift, her and Ron a gift.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:38.400
Now that'll be interesting

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.424
what that mailing address ends up being.

00:18:40.424 --> 00:18:41.700
Yeah, I don't know if she replied to-

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:43.549
777 Heaven Street.

00:18:44.632 --> 00:18:45.465
Let me see.

00:18:45.465 --> 00:18:46.298
Let me see.

00:18:46.298 --> 00:18:47.430
I'll read it to you right now.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.263
Okay.

00:18:49.260 --> 00:18:50.093
Nope.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:52.703
Nope.

00:18:52.703 --> 00:18:53.713
It's just normal.

00:18:53.713 --> 00:18:54.570
Okay, well yeah, she couldn't-

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:55.830
Don't read it out loud.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.247
Okay.

00:18:57.247 --> 00:18:58.080
"Here's our address,

00:18:58.080 --> 00:18:59.857
"but absolutely no need to send anything

00:18:59.857 --> 00:19:00.997
"if that's why you're asking.

00:19:00.997 --> 00:19:02.827
"It's not often we get a genuine chance

00:19:02.827 --> 00:19:04.177
"to help someone out like that.

00:19:04.177 --> 00:19:07.257
"So, just happy I could be there to help."

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:13.130
But she did tell me that like
her mom was back home visiting

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.530
and that Ron was stuck
with the mother-in-law.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:18.540
So, I feel like I gotta get Ron a gift.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.373
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:19:19.373 --> 00:19:20.280
You know?

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:21.690
So, how's it been since then?

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:23.850
Well, 'cause you ended up,

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.157
you texted everybody in our

00:19:26.157 --> 00:19:27.690
little friend group.
Close friend group.

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:29.070
Yeah, I didn't know you were back.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:33.781
Well, I had just gotten back,
which we'll get into later,

00:19:33.781 --> 00:19:36.331
that we ended up not spending
Thanksgiving together

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:39.660
because of a conflict
between the two of us.

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:40.905
No

00:19:40.905 --> 00:19:41.863
I'll explain that.

00:19:41.863 --> 00:19:44.220
But this put everything in
perspective, we made up.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:49.220
So, I had just returned and
you text the friend group

00:19:49.529 --> 00:19:53.490
that you took a fall and
that you are currently

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.050
in the emergency room waiting to see

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:55.883
if you broke your collarbone.

00:19:55.883 --> 00:19:56.716
Yeah.

00:19:56.716 --> 00:19:58.260
I tell Shepherd 'cause
Shepherd and I are the ones

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:01.117
that came back together,
and Shepherd says,

00:20:01.117 --> 00:20:04.627
"It only takes 14 pounds of
pressure to break a collarbone,

00:20:04.627 --> 00:20:05.516
"so he probably broke it."

00:20:08.099 --> 00:20:09.180
I love it.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.170
I love it.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:11.970
And so I was like, okay, he broke it.

00:20:11.970 --> 00:20:12.803
We don't even need to be
at the emergency room.

00:20:12.803 --> 00:20:17.190
I sat at the emergency
room for over five hours.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.303
Got an x-ray.

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:20.820
Here it is.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.140
It is broken.

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:27.140
The clavicle is broken like
right towards the end of it.

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:32.210
You know how like my
shoulders are so bony?

00:20:32.369 --> 00:20:36.090
You know, like the top
of my shoulder is very,

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:39.540
and now in this photo, it's not the gap,

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:43.618
but to the right of the gap
where there's like the break.

00:20:43.618 --> 00:20:45.030
That's the break.

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.770
So, what would that
bone normally look like?

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:48.700
Would it be, is it bent
weird right here or?

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:50.190
Yeah, like see the part

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:51.930
that's like shaped like an arrowhead?

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.520
That broke off.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.667
And typically that is more,

00:20:55.667 --> 00:20:58.413
like imagine that being pushed up.

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:00.330
Because like look over here.

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:02.490
Like, you know, I've got a big bump.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:03.323
Yeah.

